{"route":"/docs/6.0/components/collapse/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Collapse","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Toggle the visibility of content across your project with a few classes and our JavaScript plugins."},"blocks":[{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","en":"How it works","level":2},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The collapse JavaScript plugin is used to show and hide content. Buttons or anchors are used as triggers that are mapped to specific elements you toggle. The plugin only adds and removes <code>.show</code>—the CSS animates the size from <code>0</code> to the content size. Given how CSS handles animations, you cannot use <code>padding</code> on a <code>.collapse</code> element. Instead, use the class as an independent wrapping element."},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The animation needs <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/interpolate-size\"><code>interpolate-size</code></a>. Browsers without it open and close the element at once. See <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/transitions\">Transitions</a> to change the timing or to remove it."},{"id":"how-it-works--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"The animation effect of this component is dependent on the <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> media query. See the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility/#reduced-motion\">reduced motion section of our accessibility documentation</a>."}]},{"id":"example","type":"heading","en":"Example","level":2},{"id":"example--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Click the buttons below to show and hide another element via class changes:"},{"id":"example--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"example--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>.collapse</code> hides content"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"example--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>.collapse.show</code> shows content"}]}]},{"id":"example--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Generally, we recommend using a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> with the <code>data-bs-target</code> attribute. While not recommended from a semantic point of view, you can also use an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> link with the <code>href</code> attribute (and a <code>role=&quot;button&quot;</code>). In both cases, the <code>data-bs-toggle=&quot;collapse&quot;</code> is required."},{"id":"example--example-1","type":"demo","key":"39f8b51534539ae69460","height":174,"anchors":["collapseExample"]},{"id":"example--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p class=\"d-inline-flex gap-1\">\n  <a class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" href=\"#collapseExample\" role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseExample\">\n    Link with href\n  </a>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapseExample\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseExample\">\n    Button with data-bs-target\n  </button>\n</p>\n<div class=\"collapse\" id=\"collapseExample\">\n  <div class=\"card card-body\">\n    Some placeholder content for the collapse component. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"horizontal","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal","level":2},{"id":"horizontal--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The collapse plugin supports horizontal collapsing. Add the <code>.collapse-horizontal</code> modifier class to transition the inline size instead of the block size, and set a <code>width</code> on the immediate child element. Feel free to write your own custom Sass, use inline styles, or use our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/width\">width utilities</a>."},{"id":"horizontal--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"horizontal--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Please note that while the example below has a <code>min-height</code> set to avoid excessive repaints in our docs, this is not explicitly required. <strong>Only the <code>width</code> on the child element is required.</strong>"}]},{"id":"horizontal--example-1","type":"demo","key":"91d9d13bf503fdd00e76","height":174,"anchors":["collapseWidthExample"]},{"id":"horizontal--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapseWidthExample\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseWidthExample\">\n    Toggle width collapse\n  </button>\n</p>\n<div style=\"min-height: 140px;\">\n  <div class=\"collapse collapse-horizontal\" id=\"collapseWidthExample\">\n    <div class=\"card card-body\" style=\"width: 300px;\">\n      This is some placeholder content for a horizontal collapse. It’s hidden by default and shown when triggered.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"multiple-toggles-and-targets","type":"heading","en":"Multiple toggles and targets","level":2},{"id":"multiple-toggles-and-targets--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"A <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> element can show and hide multiple elements by referencing them with a selector in its <code>data-bs-target</code> or <code>href</code> attribute.\nConversely, multiple <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> elements can show and hide the same element if they each reference it with their <code>data-bs-target</code> or <code>href</code> attribute."},{"id":"multiple-toggles-and-targets--example-1","type":"demo","key":"19897e65545f31608d5d","height":174,"anchors":["multiCollapseExample1","multiCollapseExample2"]},{"id":"multiple-toggles-and-targets--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p class=\"d-inline-flex gap-1\">\n  <a class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" href=\"#multiCollapseExample1\" role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample1\">Toggle first element</a>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#multiCollapseExample2\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample2\">Toggle second element</button>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\".multi-collapse\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample1 multiCollapseExample2\">Toggle both elements</button>\n</p>\n<div class=\"row\">\n  <div class=\"col\">\n    <div class=\"collapse multi-collapse\" id=\"multiCollapseExample1\">\n      <div class=\"card card-body\">\n        Some placeholder content for the first collapse component of this multi-collapse example. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"col\">\n    <div class=\"collapse multi-collapse\" id=\"multiCollapseExample2\">\n      <div class=\"card card-body\">\n        Some placeholder content for the second collapse component of this multi-collapse example. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"accessibility","type":"heading","en":"Accessibility","level":2},{"id":"accessibility--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Be sure to add <code>aria-expanded</code> to the control element. This attribute explicitly conveys the current state of the collapsible element tied to the control to screen readers and similar assistive technologies. If the collapsible element is closed by default, the attribute on the control element should have a value of <code>aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot;</code>. If you’ve set the collapsible element to be open by default using the <code>show</code> class, set <code>aria-expanded=&quot;true&quot;</code> on the control instead. The plugin will automatically toggle this attribute on the control based on whether or not the collapsible element has been opened or closed (via JavaScript, or because the user triggered another control element also tied to the same collapsible element). If the control element’s HTML element is not a button (e.g., an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>), the attribute <code>role=&quot;button&quot;</code> should be added to the element."},{"id":"accessibility--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Collapse trigger state is represented by <code>aria-expanded</code>."},{"id":"accessibility--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"If your control element is targeting a single collapsible element – i.e. the <code>data-bs-target</code> attribute is pointing to an <code>id</code> selector – you should add the <code>aria-controls</code> attribute to the control element, containing the <code>id</code> of the collapsible element. Modern screen readers and similar assistive technologies make use of this attribute to provide users with additional shortcuts to navigate directly to the collapsible element itself."},{"id":"accessibility--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Note that Bootstrap’s current implementation does not cover the various <em>optional</em> keyboard interactions described in the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/accordion/\">ARIA Authoring Practices Guide accordion pattern</a> - you will need to include these yourself with custom JavaScript."},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"sass-variables","type":"heading","en":"Sass variables","level":3},{"id":"sass-variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable custom-property-no-missing-var-function\n$collapse-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --transition-collapse-property: \"block-size, display\",\n    --transition-collapse-duration: .35s,\n    --transition-collapse-timing: ease,\n  ),\n  $collapse-tokens\n);\n// stylelint-enable custom-property-no-missing-var-function","language":""},{"id":"classes","type":"heading","en":"Classes","level":3},{"id":"classes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Collapse transition classes can be found in <code>scss/_transitions.scss</code> as these are shared across multiple components (collapse and accordion)."},{"id":"classes--code-1","type":"code","value":"// The browser animates the size itself. `interpolate-size` lets the `0` of the\n// closed state interpolate to the `auto` of the open one, and `display`\n// transitions discretely, so the element stays laid out until the size reaches\n// `0`. The animated axis is clipped, so the content cannot spill while it moves.\n.collapse {\n  @include tokens($collapse-tokens);\n\n  overflow-y: clip;\n  @include transition-props(\n    var(--transition-collapse-property),\n    var(--transition-collapse-duration),\n    var(--transition-collapse-timing),\n    allow-discrete\n  );\n\n  // Browsers without `interpolate-size` open and close the element at once.\n  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n    interpolate-size: allow-keywords;\n  }\n\n  &:not(.show) {\n    display: none;\n    block-size: 0;\n  }\n\n  // A closed collapse is not rendered, so the open side needs a start value of\n  // its own. Without it the element appears at full size at once.\n  &.show {\n    @starting-style {\n      block-size: 0;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Horizontal collapses animate the inline size instead. The open size is\n  // `fit-content`, so the element is as wide as its content, not as wide as its\n  // container.\n  &.collapse-horizontal {\n    --transition-collapse-property: inline-size, display;\n\n    inline-size: fit-content;\n    overflow-x: clip;\n    overflow-y: visible;\n\n    &:not(.show) {\n      inline-size: 0;\n      block-size: auto;\n    }\n\n    &.show {\n      @starting-style {\n        inline-size: 0;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}","language":""},{"id":"usage","type":"heading","en":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"usage--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The collapse plugin utilizes two classes to handle the heavy lifting:"},{"id":"usage--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"usage--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>.collapse</code> hides the content"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"usage--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>.collapse.show</code> shows the content"}]}]},{"id":"usage--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These classes can be found in <code>_transitions.scss</code>. The plugin toggles <code>.show</code> and then waits for the CSS transition to finish before it fires <code>shown.bs.collapse</code> or <code>hidden.bs.collapse</code>."},{"id":"via-data-attributes","type":"heading","en":"Via data attributes","level":3},{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Just add <code>data-bs-toggle=&quot;collapse&quot;</code> and a <code>data-bs-target</code> to the element to automatically assign control of one or more collapsible elements. The <code>data-bs-target</code> attribute accepts a CSS selector to apply the collapse to. Be sure to add the class <code>collapse</code> to the collapsible element. If you’d like it to default open, add the additional class <code>show</code>."},{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"To add accordion-like group management to a collapsible area, add the data attribute <code>data-bs-parent=&quot;#selector&quot;</code>. Refer to the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/components/accordion\">accordion page</a> for more information."},{"id":"via-data-attributes--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Attribute"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>data-bs-toggle=&quot;collapse&quot;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"Initializes the collapse plugin on the trigger element."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>data-bs-target</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"CSS selector for the element(s) to expand and collapse."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>data-bs-parent</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"via-data-attributes--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"When set on the collapsible element, closes sibling collapses under the same parent (accordion behavior)."}]}]}]},{"id":"via-javascript","type":"heading","en":"Via JavaScript","level":3},{"id":"via-javascript--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Enable manually with:"},{"id":"via-javascript--code-1","type":"code","value":"const collapseElementList = document.querySelectorAll('.collapse')\nconst collapseList = [...collapseElementList].map(collapseEl => new bootstrap.Collapse(collapseEl))","language":""},{"id":"dependencies","type":"heading","en":"Dependencies","level":3},{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The collapse plugin requires the following JavaScript files if you’re building Bootstrap’s JS from source:"},{"id":"dependencies--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"File"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/collapse.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Main collapse component"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/base-component.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"Base component class"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/dom/data.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"Element data store"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/dom/event-handler.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"Event handling utilities"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/dom/manipulator.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"Data attribute manipulation"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/dom/selector-engine.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"DOM selector utilities"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/util/config.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-17","type":"paragraph","en":"Configuration base class"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-18","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>js/src/util/index.ts</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"dependencies--paragraph-19","type":"paragraph","en":"Core utility functions"}]}]}]},{"id":"options","type":"heading","en":"Options","level":3},{"id":"options--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"As options can be passed via data attributes or JavaScript, you can append an option name to <code>data-bs-</code>, as in <code>data-bs-animation=&quot;{value}&quot;</code>. Make sure to change the case type of the option name from “<em>camelCase</em>” to “<em>kebab-case</em>” when passing the options via data attributes. For example, use <code>data-bs-custom-class=&quot;beautifier&quot;</code> instead of <code>data-bs-customClass=&quot;beautifier&quot;</code>."},{"id":"options--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"All components support a reserved data attribute <code>data-bs-config</code> that can house simple component configuration as a JSON string. When an element has <code>data-bs-config=&#39;{&quot;delay&quot;:0, &quot;title&quot;:123}&#39;</code> and <code>data-bs-title=&quot;456&quot;</code> attributes, the final <code>title</code> value will be <code>456</code> and the separate data attributes will override values given on <code>data-bs-config</code>. In addition, existing data attributes are able to house JSON values like <code>data-bs-delay=&#39;{&quot;show&quot;:0,&quot;hide&quot;:150}&#39;</code>."},{"id":"options--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"The final configuration object is the merged result of <code>data-bs-config</code>, <code>data-bs-</code>, and <code>js object</code> where the latest given key-value overrides the others."},{"id":"options--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Name"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Type"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"Default"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>parent</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"selector, DOM element"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>null</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"options--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"If parent is provided, then all collapsible elements under the specified parent will be closed when this collapsible item is shown. (similar to traditional accordion behavior - this is dependent on the <code>card</code> class). The attribute has to be set on the target collapsible area."}]}]}]},{"id":"methods","type":"heading","en":"Methods","level":3},{"id":"methods--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"methods--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Methods that show or hide a component return a promise.</strong> The promise resolves when the transition ends, so <code>await</code> continues at the same moment a <code>shown.bs.*</code> or <code>hidden.bs.*</code> listener runs. The methods still return immediately and never block the caller. A call on a component that is already transitioning does nothing and resolves right away. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript/#promises-and-transitions\">Learn more in our JavaScript docs.</a>"}]},{"id":"methods--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Activates your content as a collapsible element. Accepts an optional options <code>object</code>."},{"id":"methods--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The constructor keeps the state that your markup declares. Add <code>.show</code> to open the element, and leave it off to keep the element closed. Call <code>show()</code>, <code>hide()</code>, or <code>toggle()</code> to change the state."},{"id":"methods--code-1","type":"code","value":"const bsCollapse = new bootstrap.Collapse('#myCollapse')\nbsCollapse.show()","language":""},{"id":"methods--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Method"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>dispose</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"Destroys an element’s collapse. (Removes stored data on the DOM element)"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>getInstance</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"Static method which allows you to get the collapse instance associated to a DOM element, you can use it like this: <code>bootstrap.Collapse.getInstance(element)</code>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>getOrCreateInstance</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"Static method which returns a collapse instance associated to a DOM element or create a new one in case it wasn’t initialized. You can use it like this: <code>bootstrap.Collapse.getOrCreateInstance(element)</code>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>hide</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"Hides a collapsible element. <strong>Returns a promise that resolves once the collapsible element is hidden</strong> (i.e. after the <code>hidden.bs.collapse</code> event fires)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>show</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"Shows a collapsible element. <strong>Returns a promise that resolves once the collapsible element is shown</strong> (i.e. after the <code>shown.bs.collapse</code> event fires)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>toggle</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"methods--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"Toggles a collapsible element to shown or hidden. <strong>Returns a promise that resolves once the collapsible element is shown or hidden</strong> (i.e. after the <code>shown.bs.collapse</code> or <code>hidden.bs.collapse</code> event fires)."}]}]}]},{"id":"events","type":"heading","en":"Events","level":3},{"id":"events--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap’s collapse class exposes a few events for hooking into collapse functionality."},{"id":"events--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Event type"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>hide.bs.collapse</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired immediately when the <code>hide</code> method has been called."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>hidden.bs.collapse</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired when a collapse element has been hidden from the user (will wait for CSS transitions to complete)."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>show.bs.collapse</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"This event fires immediately when the <code>show</code> instance method is called."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>shown.bs.collapse</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"events--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"This event is fired when a collapse element has been made visible to the user (will wait for CSS transitions to complete)."}]}]}]},{"id":"events--code-1","type":"code","value":"const myCollapsible = document.getElementById('myCollapsible')\nmyCollapsible.addEventListener('hidden.bs.collapse', event => {\n  // do something...\n})","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"39f8b51534539ae69460","html":"<p class=\"d-inline-flex gap-1\">\n  <a class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" href=\"#collapseExample\" role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseExample\">\n    Link with href\n  </a>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapseExample\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseExample\">\n    Button with data-bs-target\n  </button>\n</p>\n<div class=\"collapse\" id=\"collapseExample\">\n  <div class=\"card card-body\">\n    Some placeholder content for the collapse component. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"91d9d13bf503fdd00e76","html":"<p>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapseWidthExample\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapseWidthExample\">\n    Toggle width collapse\n  </button>\n</p>\n<div style=\"min-height: 140px;\">\n  <div class=\"collapse collapse-horizontal\" id=\"collapseWidthExample\">\n    <div class=\"card card-body\" style=\"width: 300px;\">\n      This is some placeholder content for a horizontal collapse. It’s hidden by default and shown when triggered.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"19897e65545f31608d5d","html":"<p class=\"d-inline-flex gap-1\">\n  <a class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" href=\"#multiCollapseExample1\" role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample1\">Toggle first element</a>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#multiCollapseExample2\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample2\">Toggle second element</button>\n  <button class=\"btn-solid theme-primary\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\".multi-collapse\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"multiCollapseExample1 multiCollapseExample2\">Toggle both elements</button>\n</p>\n<div class=\"row\">\n  <div class=\"col\">\n    <div class=\"collapse multi-collapse\" id=\"multiCollapseExample1\">\n      <div class=\"card card-body\">\n        Some placeholder content for the first collapse component of this multi-collapse example. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"col\">\n    <div class=\"collapse multi-collapse\" id=\"multiCollapseExample2\">\n      <div class=\"card card-body\">\n        Some placeholder content for the second collapse component of this multi-collapse example. This panel is hidden by default but revealed when the user activates the relevant trigger.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"Quickstart","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/quickstart"},{"en":"npm","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/npm"},{"en":"Webpack",